on-arrival: ltte_strength += 6; plote_strength += 6; eros_strength += 4; telo_strength += 5; eprlf_strength += 4; tamil_nationalism += 7; sltamil_unp -= 10; itamil_unp -= 10; sinhala_nationalism += 8; gov_support -= 6; tamil_morale += 0.1; tamil_radicalisation += 1; state_of_emergency = 1; state_of_emergency_timer = 2;
tags: event
new-page: true

= Renewed violence across the island

Reports of ethnic violence have been reported in the Colombo city, Ratnapura district and in eastern border villages. The attacks involved multiple cases of arson against Tamil businesses, homes and entire villages. Unlike previous incidents, the victims have also been from the Indian Tamil community. Many were forced to flee into the jungles, temples and government schools to avoid the violence. Police were reported in multiple cases to have either stood by as rioter's rampaged, or directly took part and encouraged the violence. 

A state of emergency has been declared in effected areas.

The SLFP will..

- @slfp1: Condemn the violence.
- @slfp2: Use our limited DDC powers to help victims.
- @slfp3: Turn a blind eye.

@slfp1
on-arrival:{!
    sinhala_nationalism += 5;
